# Dependency And Lockfile Safety

Manifests and lockfiles are coordination-sensitive. Only one agent may change the same dependency state at a time.

Root orchestration uses npm (`package-lock.json`). CreVux and WordGeni use pnpm. Some apps also have Cargo/Gradle lockfiles. Root `.gitignore` ignores `/pnpm-lock.yaml` because root orchestration is npm-owned.

## Rules

- Do not add a dependency if an existing package already covers the need
- Keep lockfile updates in the same commit as the manifest change
- Do not mix unrelated app lockfiles into a root commit
- Nested `apps/` repos have their own lockfiles; change them in that app repo
- Never commit `.env`, keys, or production secrets with dependency work
